# Reading: Seventh Position (repertoire plan: st-read-seventh-position). An original 16-bar
# reading study in seventh position: finger 1 on fret 7, finger 2 on fret 8, finger 3 on fret 9,
# finger 4 on fret 10, on all six strings. No note needs a stretch or a shift.
# Bars 1-8: 4/4 in G major. F# is string 2 fret 7 (finger 1); the low G is string 5 fret 10.
# Bars 9-16: 6/8 in E minor: two beats in a bar, each a dotted quarter. The eighth note keeps
# the same speed across the change. D#, the leading note of E minor (over B7), is string 3
# fret 8 (finger 2).
# Sixteenth notes in bars 3, 6, 11, 14 and 15; a dotted eighth in bar 11. The teacher strums.
